==English==
[[File:Amtrak 27 (P42DC) (36298306291).jpg|alt=A passenger train in the United States.|thumb|A passenger train]]
[[File:Troops and troop train (19345002218).jpg|thumb|A '''troop train''' in Canada during World War I.]]

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|trayne|t=train}}, from {{der|en|fro|train|t=a delay, a drawing out}}, from {{m|fro|traïner|t=to pull out, to draw}}, from {{der|en|VL.|*traginō}}, from {{m|la|*tragō}}, from {{der|en|la|trahō|t=to pull, to draw}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰregʰ-|*tregʰ-|to pull, draw, drag}}. The verb was derived from the noun in Middle English.

