# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[improve]] one's [[fitness]].
#: {{ux|en|I '''trained''' with weights all winter.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[proceed]] in [[sequence]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To move (a [[gun]]) [[laterally]] so that it points in a different [[direction]].
#: {{ux|en|The assassin had '''trained''' his gun on the minister.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|horticulture}} To [[encourage]] (a [[plant]] or [[branch]]) to grow in a particular [[direction]] or [[shape]], usually by [[pruning]] and [[bending]].
#: {{ux|en|The [[vine]] had been '''trained''' over the [[pergola]].}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1805|author=w:Francis Jeffrey|journal=The Edinburgh Review
|passage=He '''trains''' the young branches to the right hand or to the left.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|ML}} To feed [[data]] into an [[algorithm]], usually based on a [[neural network]], to create a [[machine learning]] [[model]] that can perform some task.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Sheera Frenkel; Stuart A. Thompson|title=‘Not for Machines to Harvest’: Data Revolts Break Out Against A.I.|work=The New York Times|date=2023-07-15|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/15/technology/artificial-intelligence-models-chat-data.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=At least 10 lawsuits have been filed this year against A.I. companies, accusing them of '''training''' their systems on artists’ creative work without consent.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|mining}} To trace (a [[lode]] or any mineral appearance) to its [[head]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|video games}} To create a [[trainer]] {{gl|cheat patch}} for; to apply [[cheat]]s to (a game).
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|year=2000|author=Sensei David O.E. Mohr - Lord Ronin from Q-Link|title=WTB:"The Last V-8" C128 game -name correction|newsgroup=comp.sys.cbm|passage=I got a twix on the 128 version being fixed and '''trained''' by Mad Max at M2K BBS 208-587-7636 in Mountain Home Idaho. He fixes many games and puts them on his board. One of my sources for games and utils.}}
#* '''2021''', Mark J. P. Wolf, ''Encyclopedia of Video Games''
#*: In the mid-1980s, demoparties were also copyparties, where the first so called hot releases of cracked and '''trained''' games changed hands. However, illegal software copying later disappeared {{...}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To draw (something) along; to trail, to drag (something).
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=VI|passage=In hollow cube / '''Training''' his devilish enginery.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete|of clothing}} To [[trail]] down or along the [[ground]].

